@@ -27,3 +27,14 @@ applyPatch({ a: [1] }, [{ op: "add", path: "/a/-", value: 2 }]); // { a: [1, 2]
 `applyPatch` applies the operations `add`, `remove`, `replace`, `move`, `copy` and `test` in order and
 returns the result as a new value; the document and the patch are not mutated. It throws a
 `JsonPatchError` when the patch is invalid or an operation fails (including a failed `test`).
+
+## JSON Merge Patch (RFC 7386)
+
+```ts
+import { applyMergePatch } from "./src/index.ts";
+
+applyMergePatch({ a: "b", c: 1 }, { a: null, d: [2] }); // { c: 1, d: [2] }
+```
+
+`applyMergePatch` merges objects recursively, removes members whose patch value is `null`, and replaces
+arrays and scalars whole. It returns a new value; the target and the patch are not mutated.
